Data Connect is the trusted, unified logistics data layer that everything else at IFS.ai Logistics depends on — carrier, shipment, invoice and ERP data from dozens of fragmented sources, turned into one model that Transport Planning & Optimization and Shipper TMS both build on. Work here has outsized leverage: fix a pipeline in Data Connect and the improvement is felt across the whole platform. We're hiring a Data Engineer to help build and run that platform. This is a hands-on, individual-contributor role — you'll own delivery of pipelines and platform features end-to-end within your area, working under the direction of the Lead Data Engineer rather than setting platform architecture yourself. It's a strong fit if you've got a couple of years of production data engineering experience and want to grow into more ownership over time, with senior engineers around you to learn from rather than being the most senior person in the room from day one. What you'll work on Pipelines and ingestion — build and maintain ETL/ELT pipelines that turn carrier, shipment, invoice and ERP data into the canonical Data Connect model; work on document data extraction (OCR/parsing for airway bills, POs, commercial invoices); extend carrier and ERP integrations and help onboard new data sources; implement data contract checks, validation and reconciliation so downstream teams can trust what they consume Platform and data quality — keep the pipelines you own within their performance and quality SLAs; when something breaks in your area, you can typically run it down in a couple of hours, not days; contribute to dimensional models (star/snowflake schemas) to a design set by a senior/lead; follow the team's standards for testing, version control and observability Collaboration — work closely with the Lead Data Engineer, Data Scientists and Software Engineers on pipeline design; document what you build so analysts across Product, Data Science and Customer Success can self-serve rather than asking you What success looks like Owns and reliably operates a defined slice of the pipeline estate, within its SLAs Ships pipeline and data features on the roadmap without needing close supervision Debugging and data-quality issues in your area get resolved fast, and documented so others can self-serve next time Trusted by the Lead Data Engineer&#xa0;to take on larger, less-defined problems over time &#xa0;

Core experience ~2 years' production experience as a Data Engineer or in a closely adjacent backend/data role Strong in SQL, comfortable with dimensional data modelling (Kimball star schema, normal forms) Strong in Python, including unit testing, functional testing and data quality checks Experience with a cloud data platform (BigQuery, Snowflake or similar) and an ELT tool such as dbt Experience with BI tools (Superset, Looker, Power BI) Experience building APIs and comfortable reading Django or FastAPI source code Data engineering fundamentals Understands schema evolution, partitioning and incremental loads Familiar with streaming/event tooling (Pub/Sub, Kafka, Datastream or similar) — you don't need to have designed one from scratch Uses version control properly (GitHub/GitLab) and writes tests for pipeline logic Comfortable using LLMs and AI coding tools for rapid debugging and prototyping Ways of working Comfortable asking for direction on architecture calls, but takes full ownership of building and running what's assigned Clear, proactive communicator — flags risk early rather than after an SLA is missed Curious about the logistics domain rather than treating data as generic rows and columns Nice to have Experience with OCR/document-parsing tools (Tesseract, Textract) or supply chain documents (POs, invoices, airway bills) Exposure to infrastructure-as-code (Terraform) or Kubernetes Prior logistics, supply chain or B2B SaaS data experience Exposure to ML, NLP, generative AI, forecasting, or analytics pipelines Tech stack Warehouse/lakehouse: BigQuery. Transformation: dbt. Visualisation: Cube Cloud, Superset. Streaming/integration: Pub/Sub, Datastream. Languages: Python, SQL. Infra: GCP, Kubernetes, Terraform, CI/CD, K8s. &#xa0;

We embrace flexibility and hybrid work opportunities to support diverse needs and lifestyles, while also valuing inclusive workplace experiences. By fostering a sense of community, we drive innovation, strengthen connections, and nurture belonging. Our commitment ensures you can work in a way that suits you best, while also engaging with colleagues to share ideas and build meaningful relationships.

Siamo alla ricerca di un/una Software Developer da inserire in un nuovo team di sviluppo presso un nostro cliente. La risorsa sarà coinvolta in un progetto di sviluppo e implementazione di soluzioni software, collaborando con il team tecnico nelle diverse fasi del ciclo di vita applicativo. Principali attività: Sviluppo, implementazione e manutenzione di applicazioni software. Programmazione e sviluppo di soluzioni utilizzando C++ e JavaScript. Sviluppo e gestione di applicazioni in ambiente Linux. Analisi, debugging e risoluzione di problematiche software. Esecuzione di test e attività di ottimizzazione del codice. Collaborazione con il team di sviluppo per la realizzazione di nuove funzionalità e il miglioramento delle soluzioni esistenti.

Conoscenza del linguaggio di programmazione C++. Conoscenza di JavaScript . Familiarità con i principali strumenti e metodologie di sviluppo software. Esperienza di sviluppo in ambiente Linux . Capacità di analisi, debugging e troubleshooting applicativo. Buona conoscenza della lingua inglese di livello B2/C1 , necessaria per il contesto lavorativo.

Sedi di lavoro: &#xa0;Firenze zona&#xa0;Osmannoro. Modalità di lavoro: &#xa0;ibrida, con presenza in sede 2–3 giorni a settimana. Orario: Full-time&#xa0;&#xa0; Inquadramento e retribuzione: &#xa0;valutiamo collaborazioni con professionisti in partita IVA o assunzione a tempo indeterminato. Retribuzione: RAL da € 28000 fino a € 32.000 , commisurata all'esperienza e alle competenze maturate. Tutti i nostri annunci sono rivolti ad entrambi i sessi, ai sensi delle leggi 903/77 e 125/91, e a persone di tutte le età e tutte le nazionalità, ai sensi dei decreti legislativi 215/03 e 216/03.&#xa0;

Buscamos un/a Desarrollador/a Senior SISnet con experiencia en el sector asegurador y amplio conocimiento de la plataforma SISnet para participar en proyectos de evolución e implantación de soluciones core. Formarás parte de equipos multidisciplinares y participando en todo el ciclo de vida del software.&#xa0; Precisamos una persona con orientación técnica, capacidad de propuesta y motivación por desarrollar soluciones robustas, escalables y de alto impacto para nuestros clientes.&#xa0; FUNCIONES: Analizar requerimientos funcionales y técnicos y transformarlos en soluciones sobre la plataforma SISnet. Desarrollar y evolucionar componentes SISnet, incluyendo pantallas, reglas de negocio, procesos BPM, servicios e integraciones. Participar en la personalización y mantenimiento de módulos core como Emisión, Siniestros, Recibos, CRM o Cobros. Diseñar y desarrollar integraciones mediante APIs REST, servicios SOAP y conectores con sistemas externos. Optimizar consultas y procesos sobre bases de datos SQL, garantizando el rendimiento de las aplicaciones. Realizar pruebas, revisiones de código y soporte a despliegues siguiendo buenas prácticas de desarrollo y calidad. Colaborar en iniciativas de modernización tecnológica, automatización y mejora continua de la plataforma. &#xa0;

Más de 2&#xa0;años de experiencia en desarrollo sobre plataforma SISnet. Conocimiento de versiones recientes de SISnet, especialmente SISnet 11 o superiores. Experiencia en compañías aseguradoras o proyectos relacionados con el negocio de seguros. Dominio de componentes SISnet: TLI, reglas de negocio, procesos BPM, servicios, BackOffice y arquitectura basada en servicios. Experiencia en desarrollo con Java, JavaScript, jQuery y tecnologías XML, XSLT y JSON. Conocimientos sólidos en BBDD SQL (fundamentalmente en SQL Server): consultas complejas, procedimientos almacenados, funciones, vistas y optimización. Experiencia en integración mediante APIs REST, servicios SOAP y mecanismos de autenticación como OAuth2 o JWT. Manejo de herramientas de control de versiones y DevOps como Git, Azure DevOps, Jenkins o similares. Experiencia en metodologías ágiles (Scrum/Kanban) y buenas prácticas de calidad de software.

