terate quickly with stakeholders to refine solutions in production and maximize their impact.&#xa0; Be the person in the room who can talk to the engineers and to the board, and be believed by both.&#xa0;

You'll thrive here if&#xa0; Have a grounding in computer science, AI, or a related technical field. A degree is the usual route, but we care that you can build.&#xa0; 2+ years of professional experience. We hire for trajectory, so strong graduates with serious LLM projects behind them are genuinely encouraged to apply&#xa0;&#xa0; Have hands-on experience building with LLMs, whether in production, in research, or in substantial personal projects: advanced prompting, RAG, fine-tuning, agent orchestration, and systematic evaluation of model outputs (evaluation sets, regression testing).&#xa0; Write Python you'd be happy to hand to someone else and can pick up whatever language the client's stack demands.&#xa0; Are comfortable integrating APIs and connecting heterogeneous systems.&#xa0; Have a strong sense of client context: you identify what's genuinely useful, prioritize, and deliver value quickly.&#xa0; Can bring non-technical teams along in a transformation, with teaching ability, active listening, and an ability to communicate ideas across a wide range of expertise.&#xa0; Want to quickly take on responsibility for high-value engagements, within a dynamic, fast-growing AI practice.&#xa0; Are fluent in Dutch and English. French or&#xa0;German is a nice advantage, and we support you in learning it if you are not there yet.&#xa0; Bonus points for&#xa0; Experience with applied AI frameworks (LangChain, LlamaIndex, OpenAI SDK, Anthropic SDK, etc.).&#xa0; Experience deploying and operating solutions in a cloud environment (AWS, Azure, or GCP).&#xa0; Exposure to MLOps/LLMOps practices (CI/CD for models, prompt versioning, evaluation pipelines, observability).&#xa0; Strong understanding of vector databases and related concepts (e.g., embeddings, neural networks, latent space).

